      "topics": [],
      "solution": "f=[1,2]\nwhile f[-1]<1000: f.append(f[-1]+f[-2])\nn=int(input())\nc=0\nfor x in reversed(f):\n    if x<=n:\n        c+=1\n        n-=x\nprint(c)",
      "statement": "Define the Fibonacci numbers as F1 = 1, F2 = 2, and Fi = Fi-1 + Fi-2 for i >= 3.\nEvery positive integer can be written as a sum of non-consecutive Fibonacci numbers.\nThis decomposition is found greedily: repeatedly subtract the largest Fibonacci number that does not exceed the remaining value.\nGiven [[n]], print only how many Fibonacci numbers are used in this decomposition, not the numbers themselves.",
